CLAUDE.md has promised `format => env` since 0.001 and there is no File::SOPS::Format::ENV. Split out of karr #4.

Measured against sops 3.13.3 (`sops -e t.env`), the file format itself is trivial and everything around it is not:

    FOO=ENC[AES256_GCM,data:...,type:str]
    NUM=ENC[...,type:str]
    #ENC[AES256_GCM,data:...,type:comment]
    EMPTY=
    sops_age__list_0__map_enc=-----BEGIN AGE ENCRYPTED FILE-----\nYWdl...\n-----END AGE ENCRYPTED FILE-----\n
    sops_age__list_0__map_recipient=age1...
    sops_lastmodified=2026-08-09T00:51:42Z
    sops_mac=ENC[...]
    sops_unencrypted_suffix=_unencrypted
    sops_version=3.13.3

What that costs, in the order the work would actually hurt:

1. THE METADATA IS FLATTENED, into top-level `sops_*` keys with a path-mangling
   scheme of its own: `sops_age__list_0__map_enc`. Metadata->to_hash produces a
   nested structure; a flatten/unflatten layer byte-compatible with that scheme
   is a second metadata wire format, not a formatting detail. Newlines inside a
   value are written as a literal backslash-n and have to survive the round trip.
2. THE MAC CANNOT BE VERIFIED. File::SOPS::_parse_in_document_order recovers key
   order with YAML::PP, which cannot read this at all, so verification falls back
   to sorted order -- and an env file sops wrote is in document order. Any file
   whose keys are not already sorted fails verification. A per-format
   order-preserving parse is a prerequisite, not a follow-up. See docs/adr/0001.
3. COMMENTS ARE VALUES. `# a comment` is encrypted as `type:comment` and is a leaf
   in the tree, so it is in the digest. This distribution has no type:comment
   (File::SOPS::Encrypted, wire lane) and no place in its tree model for a leaf
   with no key. That is a data-model change.
4. THE FORMAT IS UNTYPED. Every value sops writes here is type:str, `NUM=5`
   included, because the env store parses everything as a string. Our type comes
   from the scalar (docs/adr/0002), so encrypt(data => {n => 5}, format => "env")
   would write type:int -- a document the env store would never produce. Needs a
   per-format type policy, which touches the wire lane too.
5. The cheap part: %FORMATS, _detect_format_from_filename, _detect_format, and a
   parse/serialize/detect class shaped like Format::YAML.

Recommendation: do not start this from the parser end. Items 1-3 are the ticket.
PLAN (Orchestrator, 2026-08-16) -- nicht am Parser anfangen. Die Punkte 1-3 des Bodys SIND das Ticket.

